{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Echo-safety root-cause (live run 31816927546): determination = (A) GENUINE PRODUCTION BUG in the inbound differ's DC rich-text convergence. Evidence: rendering now passes (h1/bold/code -> <h1>/<b>/<pre>) and both-sides-conflict passes, but the converged 2nd pass computes inbound=1/outbound=0. Root cause: src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/inbound_differ.py::_diff_jira_vs_local normalizes the description via _load_adf() (the CLOUD ADF codec) ONLY. Under the DC rich cutover the local body is Markdown while Jira echoes rendered wiki (to_wire(M)); ADF normalization cannot bridge Markdown<->wiki, so jira_val != local_val and the differ emits an inbound description update every pass -- pulling Jira's wiki echo of our OWN push back over the local Markdown. The OUTBOUND differ already got 3388's echo-suppression mirror (_baseline_form_matches accepts the landed wire form map_fields_to_remote(local)); the INBOUND differ never got the counterpart. The offline suite test_rich_text_echo_suppression.py only covered the outbound direction and assumed a byte-identical echo, so this gap escaped until the real DC renderer. Fix (production): inject the neutral OutboundMapper port into the inbound differ and, for the description, treat Jira's value as unchanged when it matches the local body's landed wire form (map_fields_to_remote) -- the inbound mirror of _baseline_form_matches. Cloud/plain-codec paths unchanged (map_fields_to_remote is identity when cutover off). Adding an offline inbound echo test with a canonicalizing echo. Live test assertion stays as-is (fix makes inbound=0)."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786727900266881001,"uuid":"c9e68209-38af-44e0-831d-e7ef7816224f"}